    "description": "<strong>Version 1.1 (2026-08-01) \u2014 FULL FILE REMEDIATION</strong><br><br>Version 1.0 was published as markdown-only, which is unreadable to human consumers on zenodo.org (raw LaTeX visible). This version adds the rendered PDF (primary artifact), README, PROVENANCE-BUNDLE.zip, and supplementary artifacts.<br><br>Content: a proposal for p-adic quantum metrology exploiting passive error resilience through ultrametric geometry (Bruhat-Tits tree structure). Compares against surface-code fault-tolerant quantum computing (FTQC) on resource requirements: ~10 physical qudits vs ~10^6, room-temperature operation vs ~10 mK, zero ancilla vs ~99%. Registers three dated, falsifiable calibration predictions ([WEAK] anchors) for photonic noise correlation structure, precision improvement, and demonstration timeline.<br><br>Part of the Adelic Core Research Program (ACRP).",
